  "historical_output_text": " In the sweltering summer of my sophomore year, I found myself sprawled out on the floor of our small town library, clutching a freshly purchased copy of \"Moby Dick.\" It had been my summer reading assignment, but after only a few pages, I realized the mistake: I had misread the title. It wasn't \"Moby Dick,\" but \"Moby Dick II.\" My heart sank as I scanned the book, only to find it was a series of short stories loosely connected to the original.\n\nIn a state of shock and frustration, I decided to seek advice from the library’s kind and patient librarian, Mrs. Reynolds. She greeted me with a warm smile and listened as I explained my predicament. She then pointed out that while the book might not be what I had expected, it still held value as a work of",
